 ## Modeling Notes
 
 - **Account vs member:** `users` is the login account (Laravel Auth); `entity_memberships` is the user's link to the entity with role.
-- **User↔entity cardinality:** `entity_memberships` is N:N by design (allows future multi-entity). In MVP, "one user per entity" rule is enforced in application; no global UK on `user_id`.
-- **Owner and circular FK:** `entities.owner_membership_id` points to the membership with `role = owner`. Since `entity_memberships.entity_id` references `entities`, the FK is circular — on bootstrap, create entity with `owner_membership_id` null, create owner membership, then fill the FK (or use deferrable constraint). Ownership transfer updates this FK and involved roles.
+- **User↔entity cardinality:** `entity_memberships` is N:N by design (allows future multi-entity). "One membership per user per entity" is enforced by the unique index `entity_memberships_entity_user_unique`; there is no global UK on `user_id`.
+- **Owner:** there is no owner FK on `entities`; the owner is the membership with `role = owner`. `entity_memberships.owner_seq` is a stored generated column (`1` when `role = 'owner'`, otherwise `NULL`), and the unique index `entity_memberships_one_owner` on `(entity_id, owner_seq)` rejects a second owner in the same entity on both SQLite and MariaDB. Unique indexes ignore `NULL`s, so any number of non-owners is allowed, and different entities may each have an owner.
+- **Owner invariant:** creating an entity must insert its owner membership in the same transaction. The owner membership is never deletable (policy), so the entity keeps its owner. Ownership transfer (out of scope for now) must demote the current owner before promoting another membership, in one transaction, because the index rejects two owners at any point.
+- **Entity routing and soft delete:** entities are bound in routes by `slug` and use soft deletes. A soft-deleted entity keeps its slug reserved; its memberships are removed only when the entity is force-deleted (`ON DELETE CASCADE`).
+- **Authorization:** `App\Policies\EntityPolicy` and `App\Policies\EntityMembershipPolicy` encode the access rules for entities and memberships (owner, admin, employee, non-member). Roles that owners and admins may assign come from `UserRole::manageable()` (`admin`, `employee`); the owner role is never assigned through a policy.
 - **Numeric priority:** `tickets.priority` is an integer — **higher value, more prioritized**. Named levels (normal/priority/80+) are configurable presets per entity mapping to values; sorting uses the number.
 - **Ticket write-once:** ticket is **single-use** and receives **one single call**. All fields are immutable after issuance, **except** `called_at` and `called_by_user_id`, filled at call time. No call history table.
 - **Ticket ↔ totem:** ticket knows only its **queue** (`queue_id`). `channel` records origin type; no FK to `totems`.
